 ("Types of HSV and sites?", ["HSV-1: mainly orolabial (now an increasing cause of genital herpes); HSV-2: mainly genital", "Both are alpha-herpesviruses, latent in sensory ganglia (trigeminal, sacral)"]),
 ("Define primary, non-primary first episode and recurrent infection.", ["Primary: first infection in a person without antibodies to either type", "Non-primary first episode: first infection with one type in a person with antibodies to the other", "Recurrent: reactivation of latent virus"]),
