 ("Complications/variants?", ["Eczema herpeticum (Kaposi varicelliform eruption — punched-out erosions on atopic skin), herpetic whitlow, herpes gladiatorum (wrestlers), keratitis, encephalitis (temporal lobe), neonatal herpes, erythema multiforme (HSV-associated), chronic ulcers in HIV, hepatitis"]),
 ("Differential diagnosis of genital herpes?", ["Chancroid, primary syphilis, fixed drug eruption, Behçet ulcers, trauma, candidal balanitis, herpes zoster, erythema multiforme"]),
 ("Investigations?", ["Tzanck smear: multinucleated giant cells (moulding, margination, multinucleation — 3 Ms) — cannot differentiate HSV from VZV", "PCR (most sensitive, test of choice), viral culture, DFA; type-specific serology (gG-based) for unrecognised infection"]),
 ("Treatment?", ["First episode: acyclovir 400 mg three times daily × 7–10 days (or valacyclovir 1 g twice daily, famciclovir 250 mg three times daily)", "Recurrent: episodic short courses started at prodrome", "Suppressive therapy for ≥6 recurrences/year: acyclovir 400 mg twice daily or valacyclovir 500 mg–1 g daily", "Eczema herpeticum/severe: IV acyclovir 5–10 mg/kg 8-hourly; acyclovir-resistant: foscarnet/cidofovir"]),
